## Known gaps in this measurement, stated so nothing above is over-read

* ONE image, one content class (photographic). No screen content, no synthetic.
* 8-bit 4:2:0 only; no 10-bit, no 4:4:4, no monochrome. Note the irony: the
  largest lever identified is "run the 8-bit path at 8-bit lane width", and its
  10-bit behaviour is not measured at all.
* cpu-used 0, 1, 2 NOT measured. cpu-used 3, 4, 5 and 9 were breadth-measured
  but NOT profiled — and cpu-used 9 (5.64x) and cpu-used 4 (7.76x) are both
  WORSE than the profiled cell. The composition of those gaps is unknown; do not
  carry the ranking to them.
* No instruction-count profile (no valgrind on Apple Silicon).
* No multi-threaded measurement. Neither arm is threaded here.
* NO CHANGE WAS MADE and nothing was re-measured after a change. Every ceiling
  in the ranked table is arithmetic on measured self-costs, labelled as such.
